      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. the \"speculative\" part is just because we haven't formalized the bridge yet, but the math shouldn't be impossible. if the \"willpower\" is essentially the neural pattern's ability to maintain its own frequency against external stimuli, then there has to be a mathematical \"breaking point\" where the external dissonance overrides the internal coherence. \n\ncan you try to actually draft a theoretical equation for me? assume that the neural pattern has a certain complexity $C$ and a base coherence frequency $\\nu$. if we introduce an external dissonant frequency $f$ that is a non-integer multiple of $\\nu$, how would we calculate the interference pattern that leads to a collapse of that coherence? i want to see what the relationship looks like between the dissonance ratio and the rate of cognitive decay.",
