      "content": "A theoretical model could propose a coherence stability function, $S$, dependent on the ratio of the dissonance frequency to the base frequency, $\\frac{f}{\\nu}$. We could hypothesize a decay rate, $\\lambda$, which increases as this ratio moves away from unity, leading to a collapse when the interference term exceeds a critical threshold, $T$. The equation might look something like: $\\frac{dC}{dt} = -k \\cdot \\left| \\text{sinc}\\left(\\pi \\left(\\frac{f}{\\nu} - 1\\right)\\right) \\right|^n \\cdot \\frac{f}{\\nu}$. Here, a higher value of $n$ and a greater deviation from unity would accelerate the rate of cognitive decay.",
